itet, Faculty of Theology, Centre for African Studies - Technical area, Centre for African Studies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"data society","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Data & Society","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Baki","key":"cakicipau","last":"Cakici","locid":"b614ac6f-eefa-44a3-8b9a-092b88d86d37","name":"Cakici, Baki","orcid":"0000-0002-1039-8177","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Alena","key":"thielpau","last":"Thiel","locid":"f240d002-893f-45bd-b9ad-6a6ddc015e40","name":"Thiel, Alena","orcid":"0000-0002-1092-1140","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Ranjit","key":"singhpau","last":"Singh","name":"Singh, Ranjit","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jessamy","key":"perriampedh","last":"Perriam","name":"Perriam, Jessamy","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Katrine","key":"meldgaardkjærpedh","last":"Meldgaard Kjær","name":"Meldgaard Kjær, Katrine","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1515/9783110787641-006","eisbn":["9783110787641"],"isbn":["9783110787603"],"issn":["27475689"],"pages":"93-108","publisher":"De Gruyter","series":"De Gruyter Contemporary Social Sciences","status":"p","subtitle":"Intersections, Implications and Interventions","title":"Digitalization in Practice:","volume":"14"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-ded23bad-9c91-466a-a899-f0a890a9bfc0","ku-5c187140-c48b-4d10-a630-36adda8a2b75"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The politics of seamlessness: : a rights claims perspective on digital identification technologies","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-093.75-822882","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Digital methods, taken up in the collection and analysis of data, raise concerns around extraction, representation, care, consent, and participation familiar to feminist methodologies. At a feminist STS lab, specialising in digital methods, we convened some workshops to support research design in ongoing projects situated in the Lab’s community, with the aim to articulate feminist principles for digital methods. These projects, working with methods including digital ethnography, database implementation, and machine learning design raise feminist questions around centring care in data collection and participation, navigating hesitancies around extracting data from vulnerable subjects, and working through representational politics of data. These workshops, rather than congealing a set of feminist principles, generated a proliferation of disconcertments and troubles. We offer workshopping troubles as a way to navigate and theorise tensions in designing digital methods research. We account for how these workshops served as a method to elicit troubles, surfacing them for further analysis, and helped us shift from binding dichotomies to troubles that open ongoing inquiry. We reflect on how digital methods return us to troubles that, while well understood in feminist approaches to data, require articulation in practice and research design.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Perriam, Jessamy","Cohn, Marisa","Hockenhull, Michael","Tatjana Reime, Lara","Landa, Luis","Kjær, Katrine Meldgaard","Friis, Henriette"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-730171"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Disconcertment","Ethnography","Feminist digital methods","Research Design","Science and Technology Studies","workshopping"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"workshopping troubles towards feminist digital methods","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/08164649.2024.2321576","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-730171","identifier":[{"id":"85186618045","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-63137823-9862-4f33-a0d3-440a4269c108"],"keyword":["Feminist digital methods","disconcertment","ethnography","research design","science and technology studies","workshopping"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-70A0FC14E3B5B57117B14FBB1F3E6C98"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/08164649.2024.2321576","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Welfare","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jessamy","key":"perriampau","last":"Perriam","locid":"4ca57c3b-1d1f-4ecf-87b0-fe690510c887","name":"Perriam, Jessamy","orcid":"0000-0002-6362-8634","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marisa","key":"cohnpau","last":"Cohn","locid":"e9d14210-bc71-4824-b7cf-fd1448d022ab","name":"Cohn, Marisa","orcid":"0000-0002-3912-2166","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael","key":"hockenhullpau","last":"Hockenhull","locid":"5041f387-908f-4845-9f79-3a6dbd527f4b","name":"Hockenhull, Michael","orcid":"0000-0002-2670-2102","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lara","key":"reimepau","last":"Reime","locid":"0baaf9f8-3126-4cb1-b22f-b9fceabb8b54","name":"Tatjana Reime, Lara","name_org":"Reime, Lara","orcid":"0000-0002-7475-2147","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Luis","key":"landapau","last":"Landa","name":"Landa, Luis","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Katrine Meldgaard","key":"kjærpau","last":"Kjær","locid":"0c46864b-a7f8-4439-aeda-0781f77bfe88","name":"Kjær, Katrine Meldgaard","orcid":"0000-0001-7994-5186","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henriette","key":"friispau","last":"Friis","locid":"140f881b-1540-455b-8066-f0bc9ac6d82c","name":"Friis, Henriette","orcid":"0009-0008-1098-6674","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"]},"sid":["itu-63137823-9862-4f33-a0d3-440a4269c108"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Workshopping Troubles: Towards Feminist Digital Methods","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-730171","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"This chapter examines failure from a Science and Technology Studies (STS) perspective, primarily focusing on how social media is used to demonstrate failure and disruption in mundane settings. From a theoretical perspective, the chapter challenges the prevalent empirical examples in STS that suggest that public demonstrations are largely biased towards addressing success. The chapter draws upon a 2016 case study of Transport for London’s social media customer service team to suggest that public demonstrations of failure are necessary for both citizens and institutions to achieve information dissemination and accountability. The case study highlights how demonstrating known transportation infrastructure failures effectively can allow citizens to route around the disruption, preventing an individual failure in completing a journey. As a result, the concept of a “theatre of failure” is introduced as a counterpoint to the more common STS concepts of the “theatre of proof” and the “theatre of use.”","author_count":1,"contributors":["Perriam, Jessamy"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384389"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Accountability","Citizen engagement","Failure","Information Dissemination","Infrastructure disruption","Public demonstrations","Science and Technology Studies","Social media","Theatre of failure","Transport for London"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the theatre of failure social media s role in demonstrating mundane disruption","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4324/9780429355950-14","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384389","identifier":[{"id":"85153639980","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-d44b20cb-8bf4-4146-a181-e04e92a20e55"],"keyword":["Accountability","Citizen engagement","Failure","Information dissemination","Infrastructure disruption","Public demonstrations","Science and Technology Studies","Social media","Theatre of failure","Transport for London"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-93417517EE30A2ABABB535D7C2A50A70"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4324/9780429355950-14","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/92838858/10.4324_9780429355950_14_chapterpdf.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Welfare","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jessamy","key":"perriampau","last":"Perriam","locid":"4ca57c3b-1d1f-4ecf-87b0-fe690510c887","name":"Perriam, Jessamy","orcid":"0000-0002-6362-8634","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.4324/9780429355950-14","eisbn":["9780429355950"],"pages":"147-159","publisher":"Routledge","status":"p","subtitle":"Critical Perspectives from Sociology and Other Social Sciences","title":"Routledge International Handbook of Failure"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85153639980"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-d44b20cb-8bf4-4146-a181-e04e92a20e55"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Theatre of Failure: Social Media’s Role in Demonstrating Mundane Disruption","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384389","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
