{"abstract":"Qualitative and mixed methods digital social research often relies on gathering and storing social media data through the use of APIs (Application Programming Interfaces). In past years this has been relatively simple, with academic developers and researchers using APIs to access data and produce visualisations and analysis of social networks and issues. In recent years, API access has become increasingly restricted and regulated by corporations at the helm of social media networks. Facebook (the corporation) has restricted academic research access to Facebook (the social media platform) along with Instagram (a Facebook-owned social media platform). Instead, they have allowed access to sources where monetisation can easily occur, in particular, marketers and advertisers. This leaves academic researchers of digital social life in a difficult situation where API related research has been curtailed. In this paper we describe some rationales and methodologies for using APIs in social research. We then introduce some of the major events in academic API use that have led to the prohibitive situation researchers now find themselves in. Finally, we discuss the methodological and ethical issues this produces for researchers and, suggest some possible steps forward for API related research.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Perriam, Jessamy","Birkbak, Andreas","Freeman, Andrew"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-084259"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Goldsmiths, University of London","Open University Milton Keynes"],"keyword":["Apis","Digital Methods","Ethics","Facebook","Twitter","Web scraping"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"digital methods in a post api environment","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/312481077/2019_Digital_Methods_in_a_Post_API_Environment_accepted_author_s_version.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-084259","identifier":[{"id":"85074616989","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-75bb3dc5-4e0b-430e-ade6-1189e4d01bb0"],"keyword":["APIs","Digital methods","Ethics","Facebook","Netvizz","Twitter","Web scraping"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-66E7B816599E8B65ACF2BEF622386D62"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/312481077/2019_Digital_Methods_in_a_Post_API_Environment_accepted_author_s_version.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Humanities (HUM)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"gb","key":"open university milton keynes","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Open University Milton Keynes","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Culture and Learning","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Culture and Learning, The Techno-Anthropology Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"goldsmiths university of london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Goldsmiths, University of London","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jessamy","key":"perriampau","last":"Perriam","name":"Perriam, Jessamy","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Andreas","key":"birkbakpau","last":"Birkbak","locid":"269bb408-d628-47f8-8539-d0c4b97a9aad","name":"Birkbak, Andreas","orcid":"0000-0001-9283-1677","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrew","key":"freemanpau","last":"Freeman","name":"Freeman, Andrew","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/13645579.2019.1682840","issn":["13645579","14645300"],"issn_org":["13645579"],"issue":"3","journal":"International Journal of Social Research Methodology","pages":"277-290","publisher":"Taylor & Francis","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Social Research Methodology","volume":"23"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85074616989"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-75bb3dc5-4e0b-430e-ade6-1189e4d01bb0"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Digital methods in a post-API environment","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-084259","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
